00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:03.316
And the organizations you just saw are proof
that Singapore isn't just adopting AI.

00:30:04.036 --> 00:30:06.036
You are leading the region.

00:30:08.516 --> 00:30:11.636
I want to thank the Senior Prime Minister of State.

00:30:11.676 --> 00:30:16.316
I'm sorry. Senior Minister of State
of the Prime Minister Office, Mr. Desmond Tan.

00:30:16.316 --> 00:30:22.556
It was truly inspiring to hear your vision
such a transformational opportunity.

00:30:22.956 --> 00:30:26.396
We're very honored to have the opportunity to partner with you.

00:30:27.516 --> 00:30:34.956
And today I want to talk about how we're making all this possible.

00:30:35.956 --> 00:30:41.476
Every great invention in history started with a single word.

00:30:43.156 --> 00:30:43.476
Why?

00:30:45.156 --> 00:30:50.476
Why can it be simpler? Why can it be better?

00:30:51.516 --> 00:30:58.076
Why should we accept the limitations
of today as the boundaries of tomorrow?

00:30:58.956 --> 00:31:03.356
At AWS these are our favorite questions

00:31:03.796 --> 00:31:10.276
because right after why comes something even more powerful. Why not?

00:31:11.236 --> 00:31:19.316
When a startup founder is sketches an idea
on a napkin that can transform an entire industry,

00:31:20.276 --> 00:31:26.196
or a researcher has a hypothesis
that requires immense processing power.

00:31:26.756 --> 00:31:32.116
We don't want anything. We don't want anything holding them back.

00:31:32.876 --> 00:31:38.916
We just want them saying, we just want each of you saying, why not?

00:31:39.716 --> 00:31:47.036
Let's just build it. We want to remove every barrier
standing between your imagination and reality,

00:31:47.596 --> 00:31:53.396
because we believe builders
should have the freedom to invent anything.

00:31:53.876 --> 00:31:58.316
Your wildest why deserves our most enthusiastic.

00:31:58.756 --> 00:32:05.156
Why not? And often the most powerful discoveries happen

00:32:05.156 --> 00:32:09.356
when we approach the world with relentless curiosity.

00:32:11.276 --> 00:32:18.756
Few people embody curiosity,
compassion, and courage quite like Doctor Jane Goodall.

00:32:19.236 --> 00:32:28.956
For over 65 years, Jane and her team documented
chimpanzee behavior in the wild research that continues

00:32:28.956 --> 00:32:36.196
to these days. It's one of the most
comprehensive primate research archives in the world.

00:32:36.556 --> 00:32:45.516
But most of these invaluable data was locked away
in analog formats, handwritten notes, film reels,

00:32:45.956 --> 00:32:52.996
and observational data. The Jane Goodall Institute
partnered with AWS to transform what can be done

00:32:52.996 --> 00:32:57.556
with this data using Amazon Bedrock and Amazon SageMaker.

00:32:57.596 --> 00:33:03.316
They are converting handwritten
notes and films into digital formats

00:33:03.676 --> 00:33:10.036
and leveraging a chimpanzee facial
identification tool developed by Oxford University.

00:33:10.236 --> 00:33:15.116
They are building a very comprehensive powered research platform.

00:33:15.596 --> 00:33:20.036
Researchers will be able to learn from decades of information,

00:33:20.036 --> 00:33:26.796
like identifying specific chimpanzees
by name and by tracking their behaviors.

00:33:27.276 --> 00:33:36.556
65 years of groundbreaking research will be accessible
and ready to unlock discoveries we can't even imagine.

00:33:37.116 --> 00:33:44.676
The stories like this are perfect example of what's
possible when researchers have the right tools,

00:33:45.356 --> 00:33:52.796
and giving you the right tools and services
has been our focus from day 1, 20 years ago,

00:33:53.036 --> 00:33:59.276
because the right tool can make a seemingly
impossible task feel effortless.

00:33:59.796 --> 00:34:03.636
AI agents are taking this one step further,

00:34:03.916 --> 00:34:11.516
with capabilities to turn tasks that took years
into ones that can be done in days or even minutes.

00:34:13.396 --> 00:34:20.156
In fact, with agents, we are completely
reimagining the way we build software.

00:34:20.796 --> 00:34:26.236
AI powered software development
tools evolve rapidly over the past year,

00:34:26.876 --> 00:34:31.356
but as these tools became more powerful, we actually noticed a gap.

00:34:31.956 --> 00:34:39.836
They were generating code, but builders could not guide
the process or ensure it align with their team's standards.

00:34:40.236 --> 00:34:49.196
So we took what is exciting about AI powered software
development and added the structure that developers really need.

00:34:49.676 --> 00:34:54.036
Kiro gives developers a structure with complete transparency.

00:34:54.036 --> 00:34:57.716
And Priscilla, I love your announcement,
but we're doing this here in Singapore.

00:34:57.716 --> 00:34:59.876
When you ask Kiro to build something.

00:34:59.916 --> 00:35:00.000
He thinks through the problem first.

